/* book Worked example: Q: A site was levelled on 20 m squares (block levelling). The RLs of the grid points are: row A (north): A1 101.6, A2 102.4, A3 103.5; row B: B1 100.8, B2 101.7, B3 102.6; row C (south): C1 100.2, C2 100.9, C3 101.8 m. Columns 1 to 3 run west to east. Interpolate the 101 m, 102 m and 103 m contours and describe the ground.
   1. 101 m contour: on A1–B1 (101.6 to 100.8), x from A1 = 20 × (101 − 101.6) ÷ (100.8 − 101.6) = 20 × 0.6 ÷ 0.8 = 15.0 m. On B1–B2 (100.8 to 101.7): 20 × 0.2 ÷ 0.9 = 4.4 m from B1. On B2–C2 (101.7 to 100.9): 20 × 0.7 ÷ 0.8 = 17.5 m from B2. On C2–C3 (100.9 to 101.8): 20 × 0.1 ÷ 0.9 = 2.2 m from C2.
   2. 102 m contour: on A1–A2 (101.6 to 102.4): 20 × 0.4 ÷ 0.8 = 10.0 m from A1. On A2–B2 (102.4 to 101.7): 20 × 0.4 ÷ 0.7 = 11.4 m from A2. On B2–B3 (101.7 to 102.6): 20 × 0.3 ÷ 0.9 = 6.7 m from B2. On B3–C3 (102.6 to 101.8): 20 × 0.6 ÷ 0.8 = 15.0 m from B3.
   3. 103 m contour: on A2–A3 (102.4 to 103.5): 20 × 0.6 ÷ 1.1 = 10.9 m from A2. On A3–B3 (103.5 to 102.6): 20 × 0.5 ÷ 0.9 = 11.1 m from A3.
   4. No other grid line has its two ends on opposite sides of these values, so each contour crosses only the lines listed. Join the crossing points in each square in order.
   5. Spacing: across the grid diagonal from C1 (100.2) to A3 (103.5) the ground rises 3.3 m in 56.6 m, about 1 in 17; the contours run from north-west to south-east and the ground rises towards the north-east corner.
   Answer: 101 m crosses at 15.0 m from A1, 4.4 m from B1, 17.5 m from B2 and 2.2 m from C2; 102 m at 10.0 m from A1, 11.4 m from A2, 6.7 m from B2 and 15.0 m from B3; 103 m at 10.9 m from A2 and 11.1 m from A3. The ground is a fairly even slope rising to the north-east. */
