/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The area inside each contour is measured on the map with a planimeter (mechanical or digital), by counting squares on a transparent grid, or from the coordinates of points along the line (the coordinate method of area computation).
   - Let A₁, A₂, …, An be the areas of n successive contours at a contour interval h.
   - V in m³ when areas are in m² and h in m.
   - Below the lowest contour the basin narrows to its deepest point.
   - The capacity at a level is the total volume of water below it, measured from the deepest point, so it is the running sum of the slices from the bottom upward.
*/
