/* book exam traps: Using the map area directly. 1.40 cm² on a 1:5000 map is 3500 m², not 1.40 m²; the scale is squared for areas. | Applying the prismoidal rule to an even number of contours. It needs an odd number; add a leftover slice by the trapezoidal rule. | Measuring capacity from the lowest contour. The volume below it (the bottom cone, 933 m³ here) belongs in the capacity. | Calling capacity at FSL the usable water. Usable (live) storage excludes the dead storage below the outlet sill. | Unit slips with hectares: 1 ha = 10 000 m², so 1 ha × 1 m = 10 000 m³. */
